course: dictionary
lesson: 14786
title: A doctor's word: pubertal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pubertal is a doctor's word, and it is a describing word, an adjective. It means to do with puberty: the time, usually between about 8 and 16, when a child's body slowly changes into an adult's body. «Pubertal changes» are the changes that happen as you grow up.
explain: Use the words around it to work out the meaning. «Pubertal growth spurt» is a fast burst of growing that comes during puberty. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Puberty fits, so pubertal means to do with puberty.
explain: Everyday speech says puberty or growing up. Doctors and science lessons use pubertal because it is more exact. Everyone goes through these changes, but not at the same time, so no two children change in exactly the same way.
fact: Pubertal means to do with puberty.
fact: Puberty usually happens between about 8 and 16 years old.
fact: «Pubertal growth spurt» means a fast burst of growing during puberty.
fact: Pubertal changes are normal and happen to most people as they grow up.
fact: Everyday words for pubertal are «puberty» and «growing up».
exercise: «Pubertal changes happen to everyone as they grow up.» What does pubertal mean? | To do with sleeping and dreaming | *To do with puberty, when the body slowly changes into an adult's body | To do with school dinners | To do with eating sweets
exercise: Which everyday phrase means about the same as «pubertal growth spurt»? | A painful cut on the knee | *A quick burst of growing during puberty | A sleepy weekend at home | A school trip to the museum
exercise: «Sam's voice has started to deepen, one of his pubertal changes.» Which change is a pubertal change? | Getting a cut on his knee | Losing a baby tooth | *His voice getting deeper | Having a birthday party
test: Pubertal describes changes, so what kind of word is it? | *An adjective, a describing word | A verb, an action word | A noun, a naming word | A full stop
test: «Pubertal changes happen to almost everyone as they grow up.» What does this tell you? | *They are normal and happen to most people | They are a sign of illness | They only happen to a few people | They happen only once in a lifetime
exam: «Ella's doctor talked about her pubertal growth spurt.» What does pubertal mean here? | To do with a bad cold | To do with the weather | To do with the doctor's car | *To do with puberty and growing up
